/-!
# Finite precision for copy exponentiation

This module bounds the trace-norm error between fresh-copy partial-swap evolution and ideal
evolution generated by a density operator, including an untouched reference register. The
estimates make the copy-complexity scaling of [LloydMohseniRebentrost2014] explicit: `n` equal
steps have error at most `8 * t ^ 2 / n` times the input trace norm.

`copyPrecisionBudget` chooses a positive copy count from an integer time bound and precision
index. The resulting protocol attains error at most `2⁻ᵏ` times the input trace norm, retains
explicit resource counts, and gives an observable-trace bound.

## Main statements

* `copy_actual_step_to_exponential_reference_error`: the one-step error estimate.
* `copy_fresh_actual_global_exponential_error`: the repeated-step error estimate.
* `copy_precision_same_protocol_and_four_resource_counts`: precision and resource accounting.
* `copy_precision_actual_observable_error`: the induced error in real observable traces.

## References

* [Lloyd, Mohseni, and Rebentrost, 2014][LloydMohseniRebentrost2014]
-/

open Qatlib.Foundations.PureStateMath.BornBridge
set_option warningAsError false
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency false

open Qatlib.Concepts.ReferenceError.RefTraceError
open Qatlib.Concepts.FreshCopyExec.QpeConsumers

open Qatlib.Foundations.OperatorErrors.OperatorError
